---
// QR target for DTRUE 2026 (D46): https://nanjierao.github.io/demos/csudt/
// Links the two self-contained demo files in public/demos/csudt/, which are not modified here.
// S4 turns this into the full explainer.
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="CS-UDT demo"
  description="CS-UDT, a crowd-sourced urban digital twin for hurricane flooding in Jacksonville: a planner dashboard and a zero-install citizen client, running on simulated data."
>
  <p class="breadcrumb">
    <a href="/research/civic-digital-twins/">Civic digital twins</a>
  </p>
  <h1>CS-UDT flood digital twin</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lede">
      A crowd-sourced urban digital twin for hurricane flooding in Jacksonville. The storm replay is
      simulated, modeled on Hurricane Irma (Sep 10–12, 2017), and all community content is
      synthetic. Official station locations are real but approximate, and the citizen client reads
      your own phone’s sensors and location only if you allow it.
    </p>

    <ul class="demo-links plain-list">
      <li>
        <a class="button button--primary" href="/demos/csudt/csudt_dashboard.html">
          Planner dashboard
        </a>
        <p class="small">
          The twin’s map view. Press Play to run the simulated replay and watch reports converge
          into confirmed events. Best on a large screen.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="button" href="/demos/csudt/csudt_mobile.html">
          Citizen client
        </a>
        <p class="small">
          The zero-install client residents would use: report, take quests, verify. Best on a phone.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What the demo loads and asks for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The dashboard loads MapLibre GL JS from unpkg.com and map tiles from OpenStreetMap (©
        OpenStreetMap contributors).
      </li>
      <li>The citizen client loads qrcode.js from cdnjs.cloudflare.com.</li>
      <li>
        The citizen client can ask for your camera (to attach a photo), your location and your
        motion sensors, each only when you tap the control that uses it.
      </li>
      <li>
        Your demo reports stay in this browser (localStorage) until you clear the site’s data, with
        any location you attach. A photo is shrunk in the browser before it is stored, which also
        removes its camera data (such as where it was taken). If storage still fills up, photos stay
        only until you close the page. The demo sends nothing to this site.
      </li>
      <li>
        If you show a report’s relay QR code, anyone who scans it receives the report’s text and
        location (not the photo).
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Background:{' '}
      <a href="/research/civic-digital-twins/">Civic AI: crowd-sourced urban digital twins</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/builds/cs-udt/">CS-UDT build</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .demo-links li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .demo-links p {
    margin: var(--space-2) 0 0;
  }
</style>
